    modified_response: "I have built and launched **LokalSwap**, a regional Philippine classroom contextualization tool designed for teachers.\n\n### Key Features Implemented\n\n- **Lesson Plan Upload & Extraction**: Supports dragging and dropping or selecting `.pdf`, `.docx`, and `.txt` files with server-side text parsing using `pdf-parse` and `mammoth`.\n- **Instant Demo Presets**: Includes 1-click sample lesson plans (*Grade 3 Math, Grade 5 Science, Grade 2 Reading*) featuring generic Western word problems for immediate testing.\n- **Regional Profile Catalogs**: Pre-configured profiles for **7 Philippine Regions** (*Bicol/Naga, Cebu, Davao, Ilocos, NCR Manila, Western Visayas, Eastern Visayas*) and **9 Mother Tongue Languages** (*Central Bikol, Cebuano, Ilocano, Hiligaynon, Waray, Tagalog, Kapampangan, Pangasinan, Chavacano*).\n- **Two-Step AI Localizer Engine**:\n  - **Step 1 (Cultural Context Swap)**: Replaces foreign entities (subway \342\206\222 tricycle, Walmart \342\206\222 Naga People\'s Mall, $2 \342\206\222 \342\202\26120, apples \342\206\222 saging) while maintaining math, logic, and pedagogical structure.\n  - **Step 2 (Mother Tongue Translation Pass)**: Translates the contextualized plan into the target regional dialect for MTB-MLE instruction.\n- **Visual Diff Viewer with Click-to-Edit**: Side-by-side comparison pane with green highlights (`#22c55e`) marking all substitutions. Teachers can click any green highlighted item to edit or revert the term live.\n- **Dialect Translation Card**: A dedicated translation view featuring an editable text area, translation notes, and a disclaimer badge.\n- **Package Exporting**: One-click copying for localized plans or dialect passes, and `.txt` file downloading for DepEd Daily Lesson Logs (DLL) or printed classroom handouts."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 21880254
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
